<h2>Where should the filters sit on the account activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Each layout has the same controls: shortcuts for "Failed sign-ins" and "Security changes", event type checkboxes, a from/to date range for picking a week, and a live count of matching events. Wireframes only, not final styling.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Filter bar above the table (always visible)</h3>
      <p>Everything is visible at once, with nothing to open. Takes about three rows of height above the table. Wraps to one column at 320px.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:10px;margin-bottom:10px">
            <div style="margin-bottom:8px"><span class="label">Show</span><br>
              <button class="mock-button">All events</button>
              <button class="mock-button">Failed sign-ins</button>
              <button class="mock-button">Security changes</button>
            </div>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:8px">
              <div><span class="label">From</span><br><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Sep 21, 2026"></div>
              <div><span class="label">To</span><br><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Sep 27, 2026"></div>
            </div>
            <div><span class="label">Event type</span><br>
              <small>[x] Sign-in &nbsp;[x] Sign-in failed &nbsp;[x] Sign-out &nbsp;[x] Session expired &nbsp;[x] Password changed &nbsp;[x] Two-factor enabled &nbsp;[x] Email change requested &nbsp;[x] Settings updated &nbsp;[x] API token used</small>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px"><strong>12 of 48 events</strong> &nbsp; <a href="#">Clear filters</a></p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Shortcuts and dates inline, event types behind a "More filters" button</h3>
      <p>The common jobs (failed sign-ins, security changes, one week) are one click away and use one row of height. The full list of nine types opens in a popover. Active filters show as removable tags.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;margin-bottom:8px">
            <div><span class="label">Show</span><br>
              <button class="mock-button">All events</button>
              <button class="mock-button">Failed sign-ins</button>
              <button class="mock-button">Security changes</button>
            </div>
            <div><span class="label">From</span><br><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Sep 21, 2026" style="width:110px"></div>
            <div><span class="label">To</span><br><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Sep 27, 2026" style="width:110px"></div>
            <button class="mock-button">More filters</button>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px">Sign-in failed [x] &nbsp; Sep 21 to Sep 27 [x] &nbsp; <strong>3 of 48 events</strong></p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Sidebar to the left of the table</h3>
      <p>Filters stay in view while scrolling. But the page is only 960px wide and the table has six columns, so the table gets cramped and needs a different layout on narrow screens.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:10px">
            <div class="mock-sidebar" style="min-width:150px">
              <span class="label">Show</span><br>
              <small>( ) All events<br>( ) Failed sign-ins<br>( ) Security changes</small><br><br>
              <span class="label">From</span><br><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Sep 21" style="width:100px"><br>
              <span class="label">To</span><br><input class="mock-input" placeholder="Sep 27" style="width:100px"><br><br>
              <span class="label">Event type</span><br>
              <small>[x] Sign-in<br>[x] Sign-in failed<br>[x] Sign-out<br>...</small>
            </div>
            <div style="flex:1">
              <p style="margin:0 0 6px"><strong>12 of 48 events</strong></p>
              <div class="placeholder">Table (narrower)</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
